The '''Anuki language''' is an [[Austronesian languages|Austronesian]] language spoken by the Gabobora people along Cape Vogel in the [[Milne Bay Province]] of [[Papua New Guinea]]. The language was named after a highly respected deity of the people, whose sacred remains now rest in Australia.{{Citation needed|date=February 2023}}

